From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: carry a priority into the offload

A flow rule the flowtable hands to a driver can describe NAT, VLAN and PPPoE
encapsulation and where the packet leaves, but says nothing about how it should
be treated on the way out. Hardware that has priority queues therefore has to
fall back on whatever the packet itself carries - the DSCP a client chose - or
put every offloaded flow in one queue.

Carry the priority of the packet that created the flow, and emit it as
FLOW_ACTION_PRIORITY. The action id and its value already exist and are already
emitted on the tc path by act_skbedit; only the flowtable never spoke them.

The value comes from the packet that hit the flow_offload expression, which is
what the ruleset has already had a chance to classify - `meta priority set`
before `flow add` now reaches the hardware instead of being lost with the
software path. A flow whose packet had no priority emits no action, so existing
drivers see an unchanged rule.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/include/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table.h
+++ b/include/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table.h
@@ -184,6 +184,7 @@ struct flow_offload {
 	unsigned long				flags;
 	u16					type;
 	u32					timeout;
+	u32					priority;
 	struct rcu_head				rcu_head;
 };
 
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -694,6 +694,17 @@ nf_flow_rule_route_common(struct net *ne
 	    flow_offload_eth_dst(net, flow, dir, flow_rule) < 0)
 		return -1;
 
+	if (flow->priority) {
+		struct flow_action_entry *entry;
+
+		entry = flow_action_entry_next(flow_rule);
+		if (!entry)
+			return -1;
+
+		entry->id = FLOW_ACTION_PRIORITY;
+		entry->priority = flow->priority;
+	}
+
 	tuple = &flow->tuplehash[dir].tuple;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < tuple->encap_num; i++) {
--- a/net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c
@@ -116,6 +116,13 @@ static void nft_flow_offload_eval(const
 	if (tcph)
 		flow_offload_ct_tcp(ct);
 
+	/* Whatever classified this packet before it reached the flowtable also
+	 * describes every packet the hardware will forward in its place, so
+	 * carry it into the offload rather than losing it with the software
+	 * path.
+	 */
+	flow->priority = pkt->skb->priority;
+
 	__set_bit(NF_FLOW_HW_BIDIRECTIONAL, &flow->flags);
 	ret = flow_offload_add(flowtable, flow);
 	if (ret < 0)
